In this game, the winning strategy is to keep the number of rocks in both the piles as an even number.
The player that goes second will always win if he follows the above strategy
Imagine the final situation of Pile A - 2, Pile B - 2
At this situation, regardless of what the next to play player plays, the second to go player will win, let's play out all scenarios : 
Case 1 : Takes only 1
  After P1 - 2 1
  After P2 - 2 0 (Try to make even)
  After P1 - 1 0
  After P2 - 0 0 (Wins)
Case 2 : Takes 2, one from each pile
After P1 - 1 1
After P2 - 0 0 (Wins), keeps both in even
